# Writing guidelines

Write so that someone can find what they need and understand it the first time. These pages cover lights, heating, doors, sensors and the network that connects them.

| Guideline | Use it to |
| --- | --- |
| [Meet household needs](meet-household-needs.html) | Decide what to write and what to leave alone |
| [Create a clear structure](clear-structure.html) | Order instructions, prerequisites and questions |
| [Use clear language](clear-language.html) | Choose plain words and avoid assumptions |
| [Use the right tone](right-tone.html) | Stay calm, specific and honest |
| [Write effective links](add-links.html) | Name where a link goes |
| [Write clear titles](clear-titles.html) | Name controls, cards and pages |
| [Write clear summaries](summaries.html) | Write hints, helper text and previews |
| [Write change notes](change-notes.html) | Say what changed and why it matters |
| [States, requests and errors](states-and-errors.html) | Say what the system knows, what it asked for and what went wrong |

The last page covers what is special about a house: devices that may or may not have done what you asked.
